# The toolchains coverage is MEASURED with. Sourced by both
# .github/workflows/coverage.yml and scripts/ci/check_coverage.sh, so CI and a
# developer's machine read the same instrument.
#
# ## Why coverage pins a version when every other job floats on `stable`
#
# The per-path floors in coverage_floors.txt are ratios whose DENOMINATOR is
# instrumented lines, and how many lines get instrumented is a property of the
# compiler, not of the tests. When the Rust coverage job ran
# `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable` it moved from 1.92 to 1.97.1 underneath a
# green manifest: same tests, same hits, 400 fewer instrumented lines in
# haven-core, every path reading 1-4 points higher, and seven rows tripping the
# ratchet in one run (30833142781) with nothing about the code having changed.
# The same class of drift applies to Flutter — `channel: stable` silently moved
# the measurement from 3.41 to 3.44.8.
#
# A measurement whose instrument changes on someone else's release schedule is
# not a measurement. So the coverage jobs pin, and every OTHER job
# (rust-check, cross-check, flutter-check, build-check, the E2E lanes) keeps
# floating on `stable` — that is where "does Haven still build and pass on the
# newest toolchain?" gets answered. Splitting the two questions is the point:
# breakage on a new SDK stays visible, while the coverage numbers stay
# comparable across runs.
#
# ## Bumping these
#
# A bump changes every measured percentage, so it belongs in ONE commit with
# the re-pinned manifest:
#
#   1. edit the version(s) here
#   2. rustup toolchain install <new>      (and switch the local Flutter SDK)
#   3. scripts/ci/check_coverage.sh        (re-measures on the new pin)
#   4. scripts/ci/check_coverage_floors.sh --repin rust    <lcov>
#      scripts/ci/check_coverage_floors.sh --repin flutter <lcov>
#   5. commit the version bump and the manifest together
#
# Never bump one without the other: a version change with stale floors reads as
# a coverage regression (or a phantom improvement) that no diff explains.

# rustc/LLVM used for `cargo llvm-cov` (haven-core).
# Resolve a candidate with: rustup show / `rustup toolchain list`.
HAVEN_COVERAGE_RUST_TOOLCHAIN=1.97.1

# Flutter SDK used for `flutter test --coverage` (haven).
# `flutter --version` prints the value to put here.
HAVEN_COVERAGE_FLUTTER_VERSION=3.44.8
